      "math_academy_id": "q-161661",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,4\\le z\\le 8-x,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-\\frac{x}{2}}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}2-\\frac{x}{2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2}){[z]}_{z=4}^{z=8-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(8-x-4)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(4-x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}8-4x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[8x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=4} \\\\  & =(8(4)-2(4)^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}(4)^{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
